{"raw": {"https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/director-of-athletics/": {"title": "Director of Athletics", "description": "Director of Athletics | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.7 Date: 9/28/2026 Position Title: Director of Athletics Department: Administration Division: Athletics Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 40 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: President FLSA Classification Grade: Exempt POSITION SUMMARY The Director of Athletics is responsible to the President. The position is full-time and does offer benefits as specified in the employee handbook. The Athletic Director provides institutional leadership in collaborating with key stakeholders at the university to include, but not limited to: students, faculty, staff, alumni, community, corporate sponsors, and donors to forge an ambitious vision for excellence that is compatible with the overall mission and vision to be a Christ centered institution. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in a Southern Baptist church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Promote a culture of Christ-centered, competitive, and academic excellence for student athletes. Provide strategic leadership for the athletics department while maintaining a visible, positive, and energetic presence within the campus community. Accountable for achieving Athletics Department Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), including student-athlete enrollment targets, net revenue goals for each athletic program and the department as a whole, and discount rate goals for each athletic program and the department as a whole; regularly evaluate performance and implement corrective action as necessary to meet institutional objectives Collaborate with appropriate offices on effective enrollment management and scholarship strategies. Understand and embrace the NAIA Champions of Character initiative, fulfilling necessary requirements as an overflow of HLGU as a Christian institution. Responsibly manage and oversee all aspects of the athletics department budget including sound stewardship and fiscal responsibility. Hire, supervise and evaluate all full and part-time employees including coaching and administrative staff. Determine and administer employee work assignments such as coaching and non instructional duties Represent HLGU at American Midwest Conference and NAIA National Meetings. Act as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) DEPARTMENTAL RELATIONSHIPS Support the strategic plan of the university while collaborating with, but not limited to, the following departments: Registrar Office and Financial Aid Office, Faculty Athletic Representative, Academic Dean, Director of Admissions, Public Relations, and Human Resources. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Must have values consistent with the mission and purpose of Hannibal-LaGrange University. \u2022 Must agree to, sign off on, and abide by the standards of employment on the back of the application, on the yearly contract, and in the staff handbook. Ability to apply budgetary and fiscal planning techniques within financial constraints. \u2022 Ability to provide administrative guidance within area of responsibility, providing direct training and supervision as needed. Strong skills in verbal and written communication, organization, multi-tasking, efficiency, and customer service. Ability to work with a diverse constituency including students, parents, coaches, faculty, staff, administrators and outside contacts. Previous experience preferred in administration or other leadership position. \u2022 Must be proficient in computer applications such as Microsoft Word and Outlook. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING Bachelor\u2019s Degree required, Master\u2019s Degree preferred. 3-5 years of demonstrated leadership experience required; success at the collegiate level preferred. Working knowledge and application of NAIA eligibility standards, rules, and regulations. To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/professor-of-counseling-counseling-program-director/": {"error": "Error: Page.content: Unable to retrieve content because the page is navigating and changing the content."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/director-of-the-office-of-computer-services/": {"error": "Error: Page.content: Unable to retrieve content because the page is navigating and changing the content."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/marketing-and-communications-coordinator/": {"title": "Marketing and Communications Coordinator", "description": "Marketing and Communications Coordinator | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.4.2.1 Date : April 27, 2026 Position Title: Marketing and Communications Coordinator Department: Marketing Division: Institutional Advancement Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 40 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Vice President for Institutional Advancement Grade: Exempt POSITION SUMMARY The Marketing and Communication Coordinator plays a key role in advancing the University\u2019s brand and strategic messaging across digital and traditional platforms. This position is responsible for supporting the execution of the HLGU marketing strategy that supports student recruitment, alumni and friends\u2019 engagement, and institutional visibility. The ideal candidate will possess strong skills in social media management, website management, videography, graphic design, and photography. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Key Responsibilities: Assist with the execution of university-wide marketing and communication plans. \u2022 Coordinate campaigns that align with institutional goals and target audiences. \u2022 Monitor and analyze campaign performance metrics to optimize future efforts. \u2022 Monitor and manage the HLGU website. Work with departments and our website specialist to make updates and improvements to ensure branding and message. Digital & Social Media Management o Manage the university\u2019s social media accounts (Instagram, Facebook, Twitter, Linkedln, YouTube, etc.). o Create engaging content tailored to each platform, including graphics, videos, and written posts along with Social Media Specialist. o Track engagement and trends to inform content strategy. Content Creation o Capture high-quality photos and videos for use in marketing materials, social media, and the university website. o Edit and produce short-form and long-form video content for promotional and informational purposes. o Maintain a digital asset library of multimedia content. o Create graphics for marketing materials, social media, and the university website. Brand Stewardship o Ensure consistency in messaging and visual identity across all communications. o Collaborate with departments and faculty to support their marketing needs while maintaining brand standards. . Event Support o Provide marketing support for university events, including marketing plans, promotional materials, live coverage, and post-event recaps. o Document events through photography and videography. DEPARTMENTAL RELATIONSHIPS The position of Marketing and Communications Coordinator requires a working relationship with all departments on campus, working closely with the Executive Cabinet to communicate to both internal and external audiences. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Must possess excellent leadership skills. Must be able to effectively plan and meet multiple deadlines and high-pressure timetables. \u2022 Must possess good initiative and the ability to work without close supervision. \u2022 Must demonstrate excellent organizational and prioritization skills. Requires the highest level of relational skills in working with University personnel to meet their needs, and in working with outside vendors. Must be creative and have excellent communication skills. Must be a team player who has the good of the organization at heart. Must have values consistent with the mission and purpose of Hannibal-LaGrange University. Must agree to, sign off on, and abide by the standards of employment on the employment application, on the yearly contract, and in the employee handbook. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING Bachelor\u2019s degree in Marketing, Communications, Media Studies, or a related field. 2+ years of experience in marketing, communications, or digital media. Proficiency in social media platforms and scheduling tools (e.g., Hootsuite, Buffer). \u2022 Strong photography and videography skills, including editing software (e.g., Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, Lightroom). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. \u2022 Familiarity with higher education marketing is a plus. Experience with content management systems (e.g., WordPress). Graphic design skills using tools like Canva or Adobe Creative Suite. Knowledge of SEO and digital advertising strategies. An aptitude for utilizing a team approach to accomplish goals and objectives in an environment of divergent views and opinions. Can express a mature Christian testimony and communicate and support the merits of a Christian education. Preference will be given to Hannibal-LaGrange University graduates. To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/office-manager-craigmiles-school-of-nursing/": {"error": "Error: Page.content: Unable to retrieve content because the page is navigating and changing the content."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/maintenance-worker-2/": {"title": "Maintenance Worker", "description": "Maintenance Worker | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.3.1.2. Date: 06/16/2026 Position Title: Maintenance Worker Department: Maintenance Division: Campus Operations Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 40 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Director of Campus Operations FLSA Grade: Non-Exempt POSITION SUMMARY The Maintenance Worker reports to the Director of Campus Operations. The position is full-time and offers benefits as outlined in the Employee Handbook. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Carpentry Plumbing Electrical Heating and air conditioning Cleanup of construction debris Snow removal Room set up for college and community activities Vehicle cleaning and repair KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Must demonstrate proficiency in at least one area of maintenance including but not limited to: HVAC Carpentry Electrical Plumbing Locksmithing Welding Metal fabrication Auto mechanics Small engine repair Additionally, must be able to lift up to 60 lbs and be comfortable working at heights up to 50 feet. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING High school diploma or equivalency required One year of Maintenance experience To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/jefferson-city-correctional-center-jccc-program-ministry-assistant/": {"title": "Jefferson City Correctional Center (JCCC) Program Ministry Assistant", "description": "Jefferson City Correctional Center (JCCC) Program Ministry Assistant | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.2.5.4.3 Date: September 16, 2025 Position Title: Jefferson City Correctional Center (JCCC) Program Ministry Assistant Department: Academic Administration Division: Academic Administration Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 40 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Vice President for Academic Administration Grade: Exempt \u2610 Non-Exempt \u2612 POSITION SUMMARY This position is responsible to the Vice President for Academic Administration (VPAA). The position is full-time and offers benefits as specified in the staff handbook. The Ministry Assistant provides direct administrative support for the JCCC Program staff and faculty, supervises tier-walking groups, and conducts pastoral counseling to students. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Maintain Faculty, Participant, and Program Academic Records Administer Equipment Servicing and Repair Order Supplies and Textbooks Effectively communicate with participants, donors, outside academic institutions, and other external partners. Transport supplies between the HLGU main campus and JCCC as needed. Other duties as assigned (including but not limited to). Setup and participate in convocation, graduation and other special events Shepherding Tier-Walking groups Program support projects as assigned by the Director DEPARTMENTAL RELATIONSHIPS This position requires a working relationship with all departments on the main campus and at the JCCC location. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES This position requires the ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Strong organizational skills and the ability to prioritize are necessary. This position requires a general understanding of academic programs and higher education as well as Christian ministry. This position requires the ability to relate to others at all times with courtesy and diplomacy. Light lifting (up to 40 lbs.) in an office setting is required. Must have values consistent with the mission and purpose of Hannibal-LaGrange University. Must agree to, sign off on, and abide by the standards of employment in the staff handbook. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING A bachelor\u2019s degree is required; a Master\u2019s degree is preferred. Experience with Christian based ministry and counseling services. Experience in an office management or other position requiring position is preferred. Proficiency and professionalism in oral, written and electronic office communications. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, especially Word, Excel, PowerPoint. Experience with MS Access is helpful. To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/graduate-assistant-mens-ministry/": {"title": "Graduate Assistant \u2013 Men\u2019s Ministry", "description": "Graduate Assistant \u2013 Men\u2019s Ministry | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.6.6.1 Date: 07/02/2026 Position Title: Graduate Assistant \u2013 Men\u2019s Ministry Department: Student Life/Campus Ministries Division: Student Life Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 20 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Dean of Students & Campus Chaplain Exempt: Non-Exempt: X POSITION SUMMARY The Graduate Assistant for Men\u2019s Ministry serves within the Office of Student Life to advance the spiritual formation of male students at Hannibal-LaGrange University. This role focuses on cultivating Christ-centered discipleship, strengthening engagement in campus worship, and mobilizing students for evangelism and missions. The GA will work closely with the Dean of Students & Campus Chaplain to foster a culture of biblical discipleship aligned with the Baptist Faith & Message and the mission of HLGU. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES Men\u2019s Discipleship Develop and lead intentional discipleship initiatives for male students (small groups, one-on-one mentoring, accountability structures) Recruit, train, and support student leaders to disciple their peers Promote spiritual habits such as Scripture reading, prayer, and gospel-centered community Assist in identifying and shepherding emerging male student leaders Campus Worship Support planning and execution of weekly chapel services with a focus on meaningful engagement of male students Collaborate with worship teams and student leaders to encourage participation from male students in worship leadership Assist in developing worship environments that prioritize congregational participation and theological soundness Missions & Evangelism Help organize and promote campus evangelism initiatives Equip male students to share the gospel faithfully and confidently Assist with local church partnerships, service projects, and mission opportunities Support the development and coordination of student mission teams and outreach efforts ADDITIONAL DUTIES Participate in Student Life team meetings and campus ministry planning Assist with campus-wide spiritual formation events (revivals, retreats, special services) Provide general support for Student Life initiatives as assigned Maintain regular office hours and consistent availability to students QUALIFICATIONS Admission to an HLGU graduate program (required) Strong commitment to Jesus Christ and agreement with the Baptist Faith & Message Demonstrated involvement in local church ministry Experience in discipleship, student leadership, or ministry preferred Strong interpersonal, organizational, and leadership skills EXPECTATIONS Maintain active membership and involvement in a local Southern Baptist or like-minded church Model Christian character, integrity, and spiritual maturity Be relationally engaged and visible among students, especially male students Uphold and support the mission and values of Hannibal-LaGrange University TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT 2-3 year commitment required, depending on academic program chosen Tuition Concession for 6 credit hours of graduate course work per semester (fall, spring, summer) $500 monthly stipend + free on-campus housing (if available) Practical ministry experience in a collegiate context APPLICATION PROCESS Interested candidates should submit: Resume Statement of faith and testimony Ministry philosophy (brief) References (including a pastoral reference) To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/graduate-assistant-womens-volleyball/": {"title": "hlg.edu", "description": "Robot Challenge Screen hlg.edu Checking the site connection security"}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/sports-information-director-part-time/": {"error": "RuntimeError: posting not readable (closed or refused)"}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/public-safety-officer-part-time/": {"title": "Public Safety Officer \u2013 Part Time", "description": "Public Safety Officer \u2013 Part Time | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.3.4.4 Date: August 14, 2026 Position Title: Public Safety Officer \u2013 Part Time Department: Public Safety Division: Business and Finance Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 8-20 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Director of Public Safety FLSA Classification: Non-Exempt POSITION SUMMARY: The Public Safety Officer is responsible to the Director of Public Safety. The position is Part-Time and does not offer benefits, as specified in the employee handbook. The Public Safety officer is responsible for the safety of all people on campus and upholding all university policies while on duty. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical (preferably Southern Baptist) church. Employee must abide by the policies and procedures found in the employee handbook. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Lock and unlock buildings on campus Patrol campus, on foot and in vehicle, and respond to calls for service Enforce university policies Investigate suspicious activity Report any criminal activity to law enforcement Maintain public safety office and vehicle Enforce traffic regulations on campus Complete written reports Supervise student workers Review campus surveillance cameras Maintain lost and found property Attend training when needed Assist Resident Assistants and Resident Directors on housing incidents Report maintenance and safety issues to the Director of Public Safety Provide motorist assist on campus Act as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) Maintain a professional appearance and demeanor at all times Other duties as assigned by the Director of Public Safety DEPARTMENTAL RELATIONSHIPS The Public Safety Officer will work with all other departments on campus, as well as off campus public safety agencies KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Good interpersonal skills Must be able to perform physical activities that include walking, running, and lifting \u2022 Must be 18 years of age and have a valid driver\u2019s license Must be able to work any shift, including some evenings and weekends Must have values consistent with the mission and purpose of Hannibal-LaGrange University \u2022 Must agree to, sign off on, and abide by the standards of employment on the employment application and in the employee handbook EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING Some college education preferred Experience in public safety or law enforcement preferred Preferred experience and/or proficiency in certain things (e.g. computer programs, vehicles, and multiple locks). Must be able to pass a criminal background check To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. (opens in new tab) Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/art-adjunct-faculty/": {"title": "Art Adjunct Faculty", "description": "Art Adjunct Faculty | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.2.9.2. Date: July 27, 2026 Position Title: Art Adjunct Faculty Department: Art Division: Humanities & Fine Arts FLSA Classification: Exempt POSITION SUMMARY: The Art Adjunct Faculty is responsible to the Vice President of Academic Administration. The position is part-time and does not offer benefits, as specified in the handbook. The successful candidate will have responsibility for teaching across the Art curriculum, in one or more of the following areas: Graphic Design, Fibers, and Art History. Additionally, the employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Represent the biblical worldview, mission, vision, and core values of HLGU by one\u2019s statements, teaching, and deportment Respectful of the history, heritage, and values of HLGU Represent HLGU well, both on and off campus Prepare and teach courses Grade and return exams and homework in a timely fashion Stay current in teaching field, textbooks, and instructional resources Assist in evaluating, planning, and revising curriculum in response to changing cultural and vocational needs Start each class on time and fill the scheduled time with appropriate content and procedures \u2022 Seek Academic Office approval before changing class dates or for any class cancellations \u2022 Report all missed or cancelled class times or office hours to the academic office Implement and manage procedures to ensure records and student information is properly handled Submit grades on the campus software system by deadlines set in the Registrar\u2019s Office Communicate through the official campus email system which is encrypted to meet federal guidelines for student privacy rights (FERPA) Submit textbook orders on the software system Follow all HLGU institutional and instructional policies and procedures \u2022 Attend faculty and department meetings, workshops and in-service training \u2022 Represent the department as necessary to outside constituents like prospective students DEPARTMENTAL RELATIONSHIPS This position answers ultimately to the university President, but is accountable to the division chair, and the Vice President for Academic Administration. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Demonstrated proficiency in industry-standard graphic design software, including Adobe Creative Cloud applications such as Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign, with the ability to teach students their effective and professional use. Knowledge of current graphic design principles, workflows, and production processes for print and digital media. Ability to instruct students in the use of contemporary graphic design tools and technologies while incorporating industry best practices and standards. Familiarity with emerging trends, technologies, and professional practices within the graphic design field. No heavy lifting or unusual physicals needs are contemplated for this job. \u2022 Must have values consistent with the mission and purpose of Hannibal-LaGrange University. Must agree to sign and abide by the standards of employment on the employment application and in the employee handbook. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING A master\u2019s degree or at least 18 credit hours of master\u2019s level courses in the academic content area is required. Vocational experience preferred. Committed evangelical Christian and active church member. Desire to instill Christian values through teaching and personal example To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/adjunct-clinical-faculty-asn/": {"title": "Adjunct Clinical Faculty \u2013 ASN Program", "description": "Adjunct Clinical Faculty \u2013 ASN Program | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Classification: Faculty / Part-time Description: The adjunct clinical faculty \u2013 ASN is responsible to the ASN program coordinator and the director of the Craigmiles School of Nursing. The position is part-time and does not offer benefits, as specified in the handbook. The part-time adjunct instructor in the HLGU-PN Program will assume a teaching assignment in the clinical setting. Education, Experience, and Training Minimum of Bachelor of Science degree in Nursing Current Missouri RN licensure (and Illinois if necessary) Current unencumbered Missouri RN licensure (and Illinois if necessary) is required Two to five years of clinical experience desired Duties include but are not limited to: Represent the biblical worldview, mission, vision, and core values of HLGU by one\u2019s statements, teaching, and deportment Respectful of the history, heritage, and values of HLGU Represent HLGU well, both on and off campus Follow all HLGU institutional and instructional policies and procedures Clinical supervision of students in Nursing Courses Keep assigned students in their clinical settings Conduct pre and post-clinical conferences Evaluate students \u2013 prepare anecdotal notes, written evaluations and conduct evaluation sessions with students Attend nursing faculty meetings as scheduled Nursing Faculty Members must be able to meet the following physical requirements: Fine hand/eye coordination, oral communication, and written communication Sitting, standing, walking, bending, pushing/pulling, and climbing Exposure to blood and body fluids, exposure to hazardous chemicals, concentration on detail, and exposure to extreme heat, cold, and temp fluctuations Carry/Lift 1-50lbs* *Hannibal-LaGrange University does not require nor does it expect that an employee lift over 50lbs unassisted. Objects in excess of 50lbs should be lifted or moved with mechanical means or a team lift. Ideal Candidate: Hannibal-LaGrange University is proud to be affiliated with the Missouri Baptist Convention and faculty must be professing Christians, actively involved in the church of their choice, and have values consistent with Baptist Tradition. Appointment: Review of applications will begin immediately and will conclude when position is filled. How to Apply: Click here to apply. For any questions regarding the position, contact Human Resources at 573-629-3058, or via email at humanresources@hlg.edu. Hannibal-LaGrange University seeks to employ qualified individuals without regard to age, sex, race, color, national origin, or disability, who can function effectively within the college\u2019s mission and purposes."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/adjunct-general-education-faculty-at-jccc/": {"title": "Adjunct General Education Faculty at JCCC", "description": "Adjunct General Education Faculty at JCCC | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Hannibal-LaGrange University seeks adjunct faculty in all general education disciplines for our Jefferson City Correctional Center prison program. Ideal candidates will possess a master\u2019s degree with at least 18 credit hours of graduate work in any one of the following disciplines: English, literature, mathematics, biological science, physical science, health and fitness, speech communication, music, art, history, government, or philosophy. Additionally, candidates must be able to commit one half-day per week to teach in-seat during business hours at the Jefferson City Correctional Center. Before hire, candidates must pass the appropriate Missouri Department of Corrections (MDOC) background and screening checks. Hannibal-LaGrange University values effective teaching and student mentoring and seeks faculty members who vigorously engage the ideas, concepts, and practices of their field from an orthodox, evangelical perspective in both their teaching and scholarship. Hannibal-LaGrange University is proud to be affiliated with the Missouri Baptist Convention and faculty must be professing Christians, actively involved in the church of their choice, and have values consistent with the Baptist tradition. Founded in 1858, Hannibal-LaGrange University is a four-year Christian university located in Hannibal, Missouri, just 100 miles north of St. Louis, Missouri. The mission of Hannibal-LaGrange University is to provide an excellent education in both liberal arts and professional disciplines in a distinctively Christian environment that integrates Christian faith and learning in preparing graduates for personal and career effectiveness. To apply, please submit an application, including a cover letter and current CV, here . In addition to articulating interest and qualifications, cover letters should highlight the candidate\u2019s commitment to Jesus Christ. For any questions regarding the position, contact Human Resources at 573-629-3058, or via email at humanresources@hlg.edu. Hannibal-LaGrange University seeks to employ qualified individuals without regard to age, sex, race, color, national origin, or disability, who can function effectively within the University\u2019s mission and purposes."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/office-of-the-registrar-student/": {"title": "hlg.edu", "description": "Robot Challenge Screen hlg.edu Checking the site connection security"}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/student-public-safety/": {"title": "Student \u2013 Public Safety", "description": "Student \u2013 Public Safety | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search STUDENT \u2013 PUBLIC SAFETY Both Federal Work-Study and Non-Work-Study positions available Work times are evenings and weekends Duties may include but are not limited to: Patrol the buildings on campus (walking) at least 1 time per hour working Lock or unlock buildings as needed Resolve student issues Monitor the public safety phone Attend sporting events representing public safety Work as attendant in the public safety office Assist where needed around campus To apply for this student worker position, please complete an application here . *Please Note \u2013 Any student hired to work on campus must present ORIGINAL I-9 approved identification documents. The most common I-9 approved documents are driver\u2019s license and social security card OR passport."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/volunteer-mechanic/": {"title": "Volunteer Mechanic", "description": "Volunteer Mechanic | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Volunteer \u2013 Mechanic If you are interested in volunteering at Hannibal-LaGrange University with a volunteer position in Vehicle Maintenance, please send an email with your interest to humanresources@hlg.edu ."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/volunteer-office-help/": {"title": "Volunteer \u2013 Office Help", "description": "Volunteer \u2013 Office Help | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search If you are interested in volunteering at Hannibal-LaGrange University with a volunteer position as an Office Helper, please send an email with your interest to humanresources@hlg.edu ."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/volunteer-front-desk/": {"title": "hlg.edu", "description": "Robot Challenge Screen hlg.edu Checking the site connection security"}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/volunteer-ground-keeping/": {"title": "hlg.edu", "description": "Robot Challenge Screen hlg.edu Checking the site connection security"}}, "rows": {"https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/director-of-athletics/": {"school_id": 711, "posting_url": "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/director-of-athletics/", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Athletics", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Athletics", "deadline_of_application": "9/28/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/professor-of-counseling-counseling-program-director/": {"error": "Error: Page.content: Unable to retrieve content because the page is navigating and changing the content."}, "https://www.hlg.edu/job_ope